6. Temporal Semantics

6.1 Append-Only Storage

Adopt ConVer-G's condensed bitstring model:

· Each object version stored once.
· Version validity encoded as bitstring.
· Queries translated to PostgreSQL with bitwise operators.

This provides:

\forall t, \;\; \mathrm{HKR}(t) = \{o : o.\text{validity} \ni t\}

with no rewriting of historical state.

6.2 Knowledge State as Function

\mathrm{KS}(D, t) = F(C_t, E_t, M_t, R_t, P_t, U_t)

where  D  is a domain,  t  a date,  U  uncertainties. This is not truth about  D ; it is the structured representation at  t .

6.3 Historical Non-Rewriting

Invariant T1.  \forall t_1 < t_2, \;\; \mathrm{KS}(D, t_1)  is computed only from objects and Assessments with  \tau \leq t_1 .

Enforced at query execution: ScopingAct binds  \tau_{\max} , and the query engine rejects any object with  \tau > \tau_{\max} .

