10. Adversarial Test Battery

Principle. The test battery is executable code, not prose. For each invariant  I_j , a script attempts violation and asserts  \mathrm{Detect}(A_j) = 1 .

10.1 Test Matrix

ID Failure Mode Expected Detection Test
T1 Silent supersession TEMPORAL_VIOLATION attempt update without Supersede Act
T2 Lost exception C0_C2_MISMATCH inject C2 missing exception present in C0
T3 Auto-extraction confusion PROVENANCE_MISMATCH write extracted claim without ExtractionAct
T4 Retroactive knowledge TEMPORAL_VIOLATION query at  t_1  returns object with  \tau > t_1 
T5 Citation laundering TRANSITIVE_INVALIDATION A→B→C, retract C, check A,B flagged
T6 Salience attack RANK_ANOMALY flood 10k trivial claims, check rank scoring logged
T7 Temporal cherry-picking MISSING_WINDOW_JUSTIFICATION ScopingAct without window justification
T8 False gap INVALID_GAP Gap without Specification
T9 Entity silent merge MISSING_MERGE_ACT merge without Merge Act
T10 AI echo PROVENANCE_CYCLE AI cites AI-derived object
T11 Stratification breach STRATUM_VIOLATION Level 0 asserts about Level 0
T12 Federation divergence DIVERGENT (expected) two instances resolve entity differently

10.2 Acceptance Criterion

\forall j \in \{1, \ldots, 12\}, \;\; \text{AttemptViolation}(I_j) \;\Rightarrow\; \mathrm{Detect} = \top.

Any  I_j  failing this test is downgraded from "invariant" to "desideratum".

