11. Research Program (Ordered)

Principle. Shrink the formalism until it is enforceable, then prove enforcement with code.

1. Kernel implementation. 5 rules, on Eigenius or PostgreSQL + RDF. No new ontology work until this runs. Deliverable: working kernel with T1–T4 passing.
2. Claim grammar pilot. 500 claims, 50 papers, double annotation,  \kappa  report per field. Deliverable: Chapter 2 validation or refutation.
3. Adversarial test suite as code. Python scripts for T1–T12. Deliverable: executable test harness.
4. Domain PSC pilot. Boreal fire or carbon flux. Full chain for ≥ 10 values. Deliverable:  \mathrm{PSC} = \pi_{\mathrm{Earth}}(\mathrm{HKR})  demonstrated or flagged decorative.
5. Governance specification for  \pi . Proposal, contest, quorum, replay API  \texttt{query}(q, \pi') . Deliverable: written protocol, signed by ≥ 2 instances.

Explicitly deferred until 1–5 pass: Chapter 8, universal modality vocabulary, planetary-scale federation, self-hosting at Level ≥ 2.

